---
/** Terms of Service. Text carried over from the previous single-file site (2.2),
 *  with one correction: the retired Canadian phone number replaced with the
 *  current one, per defect 12.2. Edit here from now on. */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import ReadAloud from '../components/ReadAloud.astro';
---
<BaseLayout page=""
  crumbs={[{ name: "Terms of Service", path: "/terms/" }]} title="Terms of Service | MavelogxDigital" description="The terms governing MavelogxDigital services, project agreements, fees, intellectual property and liability.">
  <section class="section container">
    <Eyebrow>Legal</Eyebrow>
    <h1 style="font-size:var(--fs-h1);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-top:var(--s-2)">Terms of Service</h1>
    <ReadAloud target=".legal" label="Listen to this page" />
      <div class="legal" style="margin-top:var(--s-5)">
      <p class="legal__meta">Effective Date: May 2026 • MavelogxDigital, Toronto, Ontario, Canada • Governing Law: Province of Ontario, Canada</p>
      <h2>1. Agreement to Terms</h2>
      <p>By accessing our website or engaging MavelogxDigital for any service, you ("Client") agree to be legally bound by these Terms. These Terms constitute a binding agreement between you and MavelogxDigital ("Agency," "we," "us"). If you do not agree, do not use our website or services.</p>
      <h2>2. Services and Project Agreements</h2>
      <p>MavelogxDigital provides brand strategy, web design and development, content creation, social media management, and digital consultation. The specific scope of each engagement is defined in a written Project Agreement agreed to by both parties. In any conflict, the Project Agreement prevails.</p>
      <h2>3. Fees and Payment</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><span>Fees are as specified in the applicable Project Agreement, stated in CAD unless otherwise noted.</span></li>
        <li><span>A deposit of up to 50% is required before work commences.</span></li>
        <li><span>Invoices are due within 14 calendar days of issuance.</span></li>
        <li><span>Late payments accrue interest at 1.5% per month (18% per annum) or the maximum permitted by law.</span></li>
        <li><span>We may suspend work if payment is not received in accordance with agreed terms.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <h2>4. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>Upon full payment, MavelogxDigital assigns all ownership rights in the final custom deliverables to the Client. MavelogxDigital retains all Background IP (pre-existing tools, templates, methodologies). MavelogxDigital retains a perpetual license to showcase completed work in its portfolio unless the Client requests confidentiality in writing before project commencement. The Client warrants that all Client Materials provided are owned or properly licensed and do not infringe third-party rights.</p>
      <h2>5. Confidentiality</h2>
      <p>Both parties agree to hold all non-public business information received during an engagement in strict confidence and not to disclose it to third parties without prior written consent. This obligation survives termination for three (3) years.</p>
      <h2>6. Warranties and Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>MavelogxDigital warrants it has full authority to enter these Terms, will perform Services with reasonable care and skill, and that Work Product will not knowingly infringe third-party IP rights. MavelogxDigital does not warrant specific business results, revenue growth, social media performance, or search engine rankings.</p>
      <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, MAVELOGXDIGITAL SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR EXEMPLARY DAMAGES. TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY SHALL NOT EXCEED THE FEES PAID UNDER THE RELEVANT PROJECT AGREEMENT IN THE THREE MONTHS PRECEDING THE CLAIM.</p>
      <h2>8. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>The Client agrees to indemnify and hold harmless MavelogxDigital and its principals, employees, and contractors from any claims, damages, and expenses arising from Client Materials infringing third-party rights, the Client's breach of these Terms, or the Client's misuse of Work Product.</p>
      <h2>9. Termination</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><span>Either party may terminate a Project Agreement with 14 days' written notice.</span></li>
        <li><span>The Client pays for all Services rendered and non-cancellable expenses up to termination.</span></li>
        <li><span>MavelogxDigital may terminate immediately upon material breach, including non-payment.</span></li>
        <li><span>Upon full payment, all completed Work Product is delivered to the Client.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <h2>10. Governing Law and Disputes</h2>
      <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of Ontario, Canada. Disputes will first be addressed through good-faith negotiation (30 days), then non-binding mediation, then the exclusive jurisdiction of Ontario courts. Nothing prevents either party from seeking urgent injunctive relief.</p>
      <h2>11. General Provisions</h2>
      <p>MavelogxDigital is an independent contractor. These Terms may be updated with notice posted on our website; continued use constitutes acceptance. If any provision is invalid, the remainder continues in full force. These Terms and any Project Agreement constitute the entire agreement between the parties. All notices shall be in writing to MavelogxDigital@gmail.com.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
